  "Name": "SMART_UNCHECKING",
  "Description": "Allows you to reverse any pack transaction created with SMART_CHECKING\n\nThe process allows you to scan any pallet, serial number, tracking entity, or master item scanned on the SMART_CHECKING process and it will reverse the corresponding pack transaction.\n\nThe process to reverse a single pack granite transaction involves quite a few database transactions so they are batched together in one COMMIT which is contained in a TRY CATCH block. If any of the transactions in the batch fail, none of the transactions will be committed. Check the Step200 for more clarity.",
